  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-context-compression-improved",
      "text": "> An improved fork of [dsh-context-compression-selector](https://github.com/WilliamShi666/dsh-context-compression-selector) — an auditable tool-result context-compression selector for DeepSeek Harness — adding an orthogonal **code-skeleton compression gate**."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-context-compression-improved",
      "text": "[中文说明](README.zh.md) · [日本語](README.ja.md) · [한국어](README.ko.md) · [Français](README.fr.md) · [Deutsch](README.de.md) · [Italiano](README.it.md) · [Русский](README.ru.md) · [Español](README.es.md) · [Changelog](CHANGELOG.md) · [Installation guide](docs/installation.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-context-compression-improved",
      "text": "> [!NOTE]\n> **What this fork adds on top of upstream 0.1.0:**\n>\n> - An orthogonal **code-skeleton compression gate** (`codeSkeleton.enabled`, default off): the first exposure of an oversized fresh source-code tool result can keep a skeleton of imports and declarations — bodies elided, error lines kept — before the regular reducers run.\n> - A settings toggle for that gate in the same selector settings section, independent of every compression profile.\n> - An ESLint baseline wired into CI, a `test:watch` TDD loop, and documentation in English, Simplified Chinese, Japanese, and Korean."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-context-compression-improved",
      "text": "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> This project supports **DeepSeek models only**. Lossless measurement and lossy compression depend on the bundled official DeepSeek tokenizers (`deepseek-v4-flash`, `deepseek-v4-pro`, `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp`). Everything else fails open and keeps original tool results. See the [upstream README](https://github.com/WilliamShi666/dsh-context-compression-selector#model-support-and-safety) for the full safety model."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-context-compression-improved",
      "text": "> [!TIP]\n> **Recommended: connect DeepSeek with your own API key via a custom Responses API endpoint.** Prefer a custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint (`/v1/responses`) over the official-account Messages API route: it does not go through the Anthropic-style message serialization, so requests never trip message-format issues or `tool_use`/`tool_result` pairing validation (the official route's resume-replay 400s cannot be repaired from the plugin side), and you can switch endpoint nodes over time and keep existing sessions running."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-context-compression-improved",
      "text": "<!-- host-compat:begin — generated by scripts/sync-hosts.mjs from scripts/hosts.mjs; DO NOT EDIT -->\n- **Supported DSH hosts:** `0.1.0-rc.2` `0.1.0-rc.3` `0.1.0-rc.6` `0.1.0-rc.7` `0.1.0-rc.8` `0.1.1-rc.1` `0.1.1-rc.2` `0.1.2-rc.1` `0.1.5-rc.1` `0.1.5-rc.2` `0.1.5-rc.3` `0.1.7-rc.1` `0.1.7-rc.2` `0.2.0-rc.1` `0.2.0-rc.2` `0.2.1-rc.1` `0.2.1-rc.2` `0.2.1-rc.3` `0.2.1-rc.4` `0.2.1-rc.5` `0.2.2-rc.1` (21 rc releases across lines 0.1.0 / 0.1.1 / 0.1.2 / 0.1.5 / 0.1.7 / 0.2.0 / 0.2.1)\n<!-- host-compat:end -->"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it is",
      "text": "Long-running agent tasks accumulate a large amount of tool output. This community plugin adds selectable, auditable policies for reducing that tool-result context without modifying DeepSeek Harness core:"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it is",
      "text": "- **Fresh** pre-compresses a newly oversized tool-result segment before the model receives it.\n- **Aggregate** pre-compresses fresh material again when it still grows beyond its budget.\n- **History / micro-compact** replaces eligible old tool results while preserving recent working context.\n- **TailTrim** is an optional Custom-only tail reduction path.\n- **Native** preserves the Harness-style head/middle/tail trimming as one explicit profile.\n- **Code skeleton (new, orthogonal gate)** — see below."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it is",
      "text": "Every decision is recorded: stage, reducer, trigger, skip reason, and exact token counts where available."
    },
    {
      "section": "Code skeleton gate (new)",
      "text": "When the gate is enabled, an oversized **fresh source-code tool result** (for example a large `read_file`) first tries a skeleton reduction: imports and type/function/class declarations are kept, function bodies are elided with a marker, and error lines inside elided bodies are preserved. If the skeleton cannot be produced or verified, the result falls back to the original head pruning — the gate can never make context worse.\n\nProperties:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Code skeleton gate (new)",
      "text": "- **Orthogonal**: independent of the selected profile (`balanced`, `savings`, `cache-strict`, `adaptive`, `custom`, `off`, `native`). All profiles get the gate.\n- **Off by default**: `codeSkeleton: { enabled: false }` until you turn it on.\n- **Measurement-gated**: requires the exact DeepSeek tokenizer; without it the plugin fails open.\n- **Session-frozen**: like all selector settings, changes affect newly observed sessions only.\n- **Strictly parsed**: `codeSkeleton` must be exactly `{ enabled: boolean }`; malformed values throw on the runtime side and show as unreadable in the browser UI."
    },
    {
      "section": "Settings UI",
      "text": "Choose a compression profile, set the Auto Compact trigger level, and toggle code-skeleton compression in the same settings section. The toggle saves on change and shows the saved state on reload."
    },
    {
      "section": "Monitoring UI",
      "text": "While compression runs, the plugin gives you a live view of what it saves: a **compression monitor** panel — net/gross savings, offsets, context usage, cache-hit rate, cost estimate, and the turn-tail intent-summary state, with a per-session resume/disable override right in the panel — next to the session's context trend chart.\n\nContext trend for a session under compression: per-step / per-turn token composition with a timing overlay; the scissors mark where reductions landed."
    },
    {
      "section": "Stats semantics and persistence",
      "text": "- **Stock (currently active)** — net savings still in effect on the live surface; it rises and falls as compressed content moves in and out.\n- **Cumulative (across N calls)** — the stock sampled at every request boundary and summed; answers \"how much was saved historically\" and survives host restarts.\n- **Money saved** — cumulative weighted by cache hit/miss at official list prices (deepseek-official official routes only; other routes show the token figure)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Stats semantics and persistence",
      "text": "Stats persist in SQLite (`~/.dsh/storages/dsh-context-compression/stats.sqlite`) across host restarts; a missing driver or write failure degrades visibly (panel badge, in-memory fallback). Historical sessions are backfilled from on-disk behavior records (host `sessionQuery` service preferred, read-only session-log parsing as fallback — session files are never written). Records contain counts, sequence numbers, session identifiers, and enum component names only; original text and free-form text never enter the database. Delete the file to reset stats completely."
    },
    {
      "section": "Stats semantics and persistence",
      "text": "The `/ccip` command drives the panel in real time: `rows stock|total|money on|off`, `mode compact|full`, `session <id|latest|off>`, `flush`, `backfill pause|resume|status`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "**Recommended: install from npm.** One version covers every supported Harness line — `latest` carries the full 17-rc enum (0.1.0-rc.2 → 0.2.1-rc.2); the runtime picks per-line code paths on its own.\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-context-compression-improved@latest\ndsh --profile web --dump-config\n```\n\nFrom source (alternative — the internal package names intentionally stay upstream's):"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/drscrewdriver/dsh-context-compression-improved.git\ncd dsh-context-compression-improved\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm build\n\nThen pack the selector package and add it to a Harness profile — the full walkthrough, including verification and uninstall steps, is in the [installation guide](docs/installation.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm lint          # ESLint baseline (also enforced in CI)\npnpm typecheck     # runtime + selector + tests tsc, plus the bundle step\npnpm test          # full vitest suite\n\nContributions follow the upstream discipline: add the failing regression first, keep every production change inside this repository, and explain “triggered”, “enabled but skipped”, and fail-open evidence separately. See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "- Built and tested against the official DeepSeek Harness releases; peers declare the full supported-hosts enum (`0.1.0-rc.2` → `0.2.1-rc.2`, seven lines) and the plugin uses public plugin and profile APIs only. The supported list is generated into the managed block above by `scripts/sync-hosts.mjs` from `scripts/hosts.mjs`.\n- Requires Node `^22.19.0 || >=24` and pnpm `11.7.0`.\n- The plugin uses only public Harness extension APIs and does not modify Harness core code. Unofficial community project, not affiliated with or endorsed by DeepSeek."
    },
    {
      "section": "Credits and license",
      "text": "- Upstream project and all prior work: [WilliamShi666/dsh-context-compression-selector](https://github.com/WilliamShi666/dsh-context-compression-selector) by WilliamShi666 (MIT).\n- Fork additions (code-skeleton gate, tooling, localized docs): drscrewdriver.\n- MIT — see [LICENSE](LICENSE) (upstream copyright notice retained) and [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) for bundled tokenizer provenance."
    }
  ],
